UID:3e13083b823bc68c@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART:20260922T130000Z
DTEND:20260922T150000Z
SUMMARY:Police Reforms – 20 years
LOCATION:Seminar Rooms 1\,2\,3\, India International Centre\, 40 Max Muel
 ler Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/police-reforms-20-years
DESCRIPTION:Chair: Justice Vineet Saran\, former Judge\, Supreme Court of
  India\nDiscussants: Prakash Singh\, Former Director General BSF\, DGP UP
 \, and DGP Assam\; G K Pillai\, Former Home Secretary\; and Vipul Mudgal\
 , Director Common Cause\nThe British left behind a colonial police struct
 ure at the time of Independence\, which continues nearly eight decades la
 ter. Despite the Supreme Court’s directions of September 22\, 2006 for 
 comprehensive police reforms\, implementation by the states has remained 
 largely half-hearted. Police reforms are a must for a progressive India. 
 The vision of a Viksit Bharat cannot be achieved without the solid founda
 tion of good law and order\, which only a professional police force uphol
 ding the rule of law can provide. Twenty years after the judicial directi
 ons\, it is essential that the campaign for police reforms is sustained a
 nd given greater impetus.\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/police-reform
 s-20-years
CATEGORIES:talk
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:00e8b698926032a8@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART:20260922T133000Z
DTEND:20260922T153000Z
SUMMARY:IHC Theatre Festival 2026. The Tragedy of Ham MacLear
LOCATION:The Stein Auditorium\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New D
 elhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1416
DESCRIPTION:IHC Theatre Festival 2026 . The Tragedy of Ham MacLear (Engli
 sh/65 mins) Wri. & Dir. Akash Khurana . Cast. Akash Khurana\, Garima Yajn
 ik & Mantra . Ham MacLear\, a passionate Shakespeare veteran\, begins to 
 struggle with dementia. His long-time companions\, Busker and Chorus\, mu
 st navigate the delicate balance between honouring his legacy and ensurin
 g his well-being. As Ham begins to confuse reality with his beloved plays
 \, their clever and heartwarming attempts to help him bring the trio face
 -to-face with the harsh realities of ageing and the inevitability of chan
 ge. A poignant exploration of love\, friendship\, and the enduring power 
 of the arts\, even in the face of life’s most challenging obstacles. Pr
 od. Akvarious Productions . Tickets at Rs.200\, Rs.350\, & Rs.500 are ava
 ilable on bookmyshow.com and at the Habitat Programmes desk. Late entry i
 s strictly prohibited .\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1416
CATEGORIES:performance\,theatre
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d67b93bbbd3be974@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260920T105600Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Raj Se Swaraj Tak From Colonial Rule to Freedom- Through the Eyes
  of Shekhawati
LOCATION:Visual Arts Gallery\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New De
 lhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Exhibitions_Details
DESCRIPTION:To mark India’s 80th year of Independence\, MOHAR (Museum o
 f Heritage and Art at Ramgarh) presents “Raj Se Swaraj Tak”\, an imme
 rse eight-day journey of pre-independence and Post independence India in 
 the 1800s and 1900s\, through the discoveries in the Havelies of the Shek
 hawati Seths\, who created the magical frescoed region of Shekhawati\, ca
 lled the “Open-air Art gallery of Rajasthan”.\nThe exhibition and oth
 er events will showcase cultural narratives and lifestyles through the wa
 ll frescoes of Shekhawati\, the art and design influences\, belief system
 s\, religious and folk stories\, the British influence\, political art\, 
 lifestyle secrets\, architecture\, attire\, objects created or acquired b
 y the Shekhawati Seths - Art\, Media\, Manuscripts\, Telegrams\, Newspape
 rs\, Letters\, Maps\, spectacular oleographs\,\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.or
 g/Exhibitions_Details
CATEGORIES:exhibition\,art\,history
END:VEVENT
