SUMMARY:IHC Theatre Festival 2026. Bhasbharatam
LOCATION:The Stein Auditorium\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New D
 elhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1426
DESCRIPTION:IHC Theatre Festival 2026 . Bhasbharatam (Hindi/110 mins) Wri
 . Mahakavi Bhasa . Playwright Asif Ali . Dir. Piyal Bhattacharya . A trad
 itional storytelling performance based on Bhasa’s Mahabharata\, narrate
 d through Charan and Bhatta\, the ancient narrators of India. Through fiv
 e classic Sanskrit plays of Bhasa— Pancharatram\, Dootvakyam\, Karnabha
 ram\, Dutaghatotkacha\, and Urubhangam —the production journeys through
  key moments of the Mahabharata: exile\, peace attempts\, war\, and final
  redemption. Bookended by the Bharat Vakya\, preaching the enduring value
  of wisdom. Prod. National School of Drama\, Sikkim Repertory Company . T
 ickets at Rs.200\, Rs.350\, & Rs.500 are available on bookmyshow.com and 
 at the Habitat Programmes desk . Late entry is strictly prohibited .\n\nh
 ttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1426
